    "sectionTitle": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "description": "ICE catheters are used for visualization of cardiac anatomy as well as other devices within the heart. ICE catheters can typically be found in EP labs and Cath labs. Stryker’s Sustainability Solutions offer 2D and 3D ICE catheters. ICE imaging provides direct visualization of the pulmonary veins and other anatomical landmarks. They also assist in guiding the transeptal puncture itself. ",
